          <ownedRelationship xsi:type="sysml:OwningMembership" xmi:id="69529741-cfa4-5946-9d64-dc3c087abd90" elementId="69529741-cfa4-5946-9d64-dc3c087abd90">
            <ownedRelatedElement xsi:type="sysml:Documentation" xmi:id="75110993-0d16-5a25-b8fc-56a4825c49f5" elementId="75110993-0d16-5a25-b8fc-56a4825c49f5" body="source: item 9-27.2 osmotic factor of solvent, osmotic coefficient of solvent A&#xA;symbol(s): `&#x3c6;`&#xA;application domain: generic&#xA;name: OsmoticFactorOfSolvent (specializes DimensionOneQuantity)&#xA;quantity dimension: 1&#xA;measurement unit(s): 1&#xA;tensor order: 0&#xA;definition: quantity given by: `&#x3c6; = -(M_A sum b_B)^-1 ln(a_A)` where `M_A` is the molar mass (item 9-4) of the solvent A, &#x2211; denotes summation over all the solutes, `b_B` is the molality of solute B (item 9-15), and `a_A` is the activity of solvent A (item 9-27.1)&#xA;remarks: The name &quot;osmotic coefficient&quot; is generally used, although the name &quot;osmotic factor&quot; is more systematic. This concept especially applies to a dilute liquid solution.&#xA;"/>
          </ownedRelationship>
        </ownedRelatedElement>
      </ownedRelationship>
      <ownedRelationship xsi:type="sysml:OwningMembership" xmi:id="7225bdf9-16dd-5e22-b157-c9f628da448b" elementId="7225bdf9-16dd-5e22-b157-c9f628da448b">
